From 925e86e6b2ec729e5077cae7efd63beba3d67bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:54:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check Qdrant against the chunk jsonl: startup checks and
 qdrant pytests

db_ops/verify.py holds the checks (no models loaded, nothing exits): point
counts (total, then per document on a mismatch), collection config, the
sectors payload index, chunk id / point id sets, payload equality, and a
vector freshness canary that re-embeds a random sample and compares it with
what is stored. `mrr embed` only embeds ids it has not seen, so a changed
model or build_embedding_text was previously invisible.

The app now refuses to start when the point count or vector config does not
match the chunk jsonl (and says to run mrr embed); a missing sectors index
only warns. build_embedding_text moves to db_ops/utils.py so verify can share
it without importing embed.py, which loads models at import.

Tests: verify logic against an in-memory Qdrant with fake models, the
startup check, and a `qdrant` marked file that checks the real collection
(skipped by default and when Qdrant is unreachable; run with -m qdrant).

